{"name":"Borderline Pink","hex":"#ee1166","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"borderline","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Nearly; not clearly on one side or the other of a border or boundary, ambiguous.","Of questionable taste or acceptability; approaching bad taste."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Nearly; not entirely but nevertheless to a great extent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/borderline"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Borderline (Madonna song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Borderline\" is a song recorded by the American singer Madonna for her 1983 self-titled debut album. Written and produced by Reggie Lucas and recorded at Sigma Sound Studios in New York City, it is a pop song with R&B influences and elements of 1970s disco and Philadelphia soul. Its lyrics portray an unequal relationship in which the narrator remains drawn to an emotionally detached partner."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Madonna_-_Borderline_%28US_7-inch_single%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borderline_(Madonna_song)","wikidata":"Q893426"},{"title":"Borderline (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Borderline was an early-1970s band from Woodstock, New York, that fused elements of folk, rock, country and jazz. Consisting of brothers David Gershen and Jon Gershen as well as Jim Rooney, the trio recorded two albums, the second of which was not officially released until 2001, and then only in Japan, due to record company problems. Though the group did not enjoy a great deal of commercial success, it was part of the \"Woodstock scene\" of the early 1970s that included Van Morrison and the Band. Borderline was a forerunner of musical artists who would eventually be grouped under the \"Americana\" genre. Also notable is that their two albums featured some well-known backing musicians including members of the Band. After Borderline broke up in 1974, the Gershen brothers pursued various projects while Rooney became a successful producer in Nashville, working with artists including Iris DeMent, Nanci Griffith and John Prine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Borderline1974.jpg/330px-Borderline1974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borderline_(band)","wikidata":"Q16823878"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/BillyOcean_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-BillyOcean_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/BillyOcean_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-BillyOcean_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"When the Going Gets Tough, the Tough Get Going\" by Billy Ocean (pictured in 1987) kept \"Borderline\" from reaching number one on the UK Singles Chart during its 1986 re-release.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABillyOcean_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Madonna_-_Tears_of_a_clown_%2826193877232%29.jpg/500px-Madonna_-_Tears_of_a_clown_%2826193877232%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Madonna_-_Tears_of_a_clown_%2826193877232%29.jpg/1280px-Madonna_-_Tears_of_a_clown_%2826193877232%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Madonna_-_Tears_of_a_clown_%2826193877232%29.jpg/500px-Madonna_-_Tears_of_a_clown_%2826193877232%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Madonna singing \"Borderline\" on her Tears of a Clown show.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadonna_-_Tears_of_a_clown_(26193877232).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Duffy_%40_Super_Bock_Super_Rock_01.jpg/500px-Duffy_%40_Super_Bock_Super_Rock_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Duffy_%40_Super_Bock_Super_Rock_01.jpg/500px-Duffy_%40_Super_Bock_Super_Rock_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADuffy_%40_Super_Bock_Super_Rock_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Jody_Watley_Capital_Pride_-_10.jpg/500px-Jody_Watley_Capital_Pride_-_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Jody_Watley_Capital_Pride_-_10.jpg/500px-Jody_Watley_Capital_Pride_-_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJody_Watley_Capital_Pride_-_10.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wik